            <description><![CDATA[ &lt;h2 id=&#34;Mendeley-GB-T-7714-2005&#34;&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#Mendeley-GB-T-7714-2005&#34; class=&#34;headerlink&#34; title=&#34;Mendeley GB/T 7714-2005&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Mendeley GB/T 7714-2005&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;For English references, author names were shown in all caps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;For English references with more than three authors, the Chinese “等” was used for omission instead of “et al.”&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://blog.csdn.net/yitian_z/article/details/104050142&#34;&gt;Solution&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I configured my own reference format and am sharing it here. Its features include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remove &lt;code&gt;//&lt;/code&gt; from references, especially the extra separator after conference names&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;Citing-CNKI-References&#34;&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#Citing-CNKI-References&#34; class=&#34;headerlink&#34; title=&#34;Citing CNKI References&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Citing CNKI References&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;CNKI does not provide a Bib reference format supported by Mendeley, so I wrote a website that can convert references online: &lt;a href=&#34;https://cnki2bib.youngforest.me/products&#34;&gt;Entrance 1&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;https://youngforest.me/products&#34;&gt;Entrance 2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
 ]]></description>
